=== counters and fixed text
[0] [1] [1] [wbsh]
\l ok
=== \nnn is an octal character code; \\ a backslash; unknown escapes stay
ABC \ \q !1
=== the date and time escapes
times ok
\D{%Y} ok
\D{} is the locale time
\D
=== the version escapes
versions ok
=== \$ is $, or # in an elevated shell
\$ ok
=== promptvars: parameter, command and arithmetic expansion after the escapes
hello world cmd 42 back
\u then $name ok
=== text from an escape is not expanded again
prompt_$HOME_dir
=== a backslash quotes $ ` " and itself in the expansion
a$b `c` "d" e\f
=== with promptvars off only the escapes are decoded
$name $ A
promptvars      off
=== an interactive shell: PS1 expansion, \#, \!, PROMPT_COMMAND
[1:1:2]$ one
[2:2:2]$ two
[3:3:2]$ 
(exit 0)
--- $? is not changed by the prompt's command substitution
[]$ []$ status=1
[]$ []$ status=0
[]$ 
(exit 0)
--- PROMPT_COMMAND runs before each primary prompt and keeps $?
[p]$ <pc>
[p]$ <pc>
[p]$ status=1
<pc>
[p]$ 
(exit 0)
--- an array PROMPT_COMMAND runs every element
[p]$ first
second
[p]$ body
first
second
[p]$ 
(exit 0)
--- PROMPT_COMMAND is not run before a continuation prompt
[p]$ <pc>
[p]$ > > inside
<pc>
[p]$ 
(exit 0)
--- exit in PROMPT_COMMAND ends the shell
[p]$ (exit 7)
